From: hmaarrfk <mark.harfouche@conda-forge.org>
Date: 2026-06-02
Subject: relax -Werror=missing-field-initializers for newer Level Zero headers

This driver targets Level Zero 1.27.0 (cmake/level-zero.cmake), but the
recipe builds it against the conda-forge `level-zero` package, currently
1.29.0, so that the userspace driver matches the loader it is dlopened
by at runtime. The newer loader headers add members to the Level Zero
DDI tables (e.g. ze_command_list_dditable_t::pfnAppendMemoryCopyWith-
Parameters, ze_device_dditable_t::pfnGetRuntimeRequirements). The driver
fills those tables with designated initializers that only name the
entries it implements, so the new members are value-initialized to null:

    umd/level_zero_driver/api/ze_cmdlist.cpp:658: error: missing
      initializer for member
      '_ze_command_list_dditable_t::pfnAppendMemoryCopyWithParameters'
      [-Werror=missing-field-initializers]

Leaving those entries null is correct — they are functions this driver
predates, and the loader treats a null entry as unsupported. Only the
combination with -Werror (cmake/compiler_flags.cmake) turns the warning
into a build failure. Keep the warning but drop it back to non-fatal
with -Wno-error=missing-field-initializers, rather than pinning the host
to an older level-zero than the one users will run against.

Paths in this patch are prefixed with `linux-npu-driver/`
because the recipe extracts this source into an explicit
`target_directory`, so patches are applied from one level above the
upstream root.
---
 linux-npu-driver/cmake/compiler_flags.cmake | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)
diff --git a/linux-npu-driver/cmake/compiler_flags.cmake b/linux-npu-driver/cmake/compiler_flags.cmake
index 0cc74c7..cfd1715 100644
--- a/linux-npu-driver/cmake/compiler_flags.cmake
+++ b/linux-npu-driver/cmake/compiler_flags.cmake
@@ -5,6 +5,12 @@
 add_compile_options(
   # Compiler warnings
   -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Wno-unused-parameter -Wvla -Wno-error=cpp
+  # The Level Zero loader headers we build against (conda-forge
+  # level-zero) are newer than the version this driver targets, so the
+  # DDI tables it fills have members it does not initialize. Those are
+  # intentionally left null (features this driver predates); keep the
+  # warning but do not let -Werror turn it into a hard failure.
+  -Wno-error=missing-field-initializers
   # Control flow integrity
   $<$<CONFIG:Release>:-fcf-protection=full>
   # Format string defence
